# Value icon colors — one map only

Filter-by-value tiles and Project Outlines table **ICONS** badges must be pixel-identical in color for each icon id.

## Source of truth

- `index.html` `:root` → `--vi-{id}-bg`, `--vi-{id}-fg`, `--vi-{id}-border` (and `-chip` for filter button soft tint)
- Applied via `.value-icon.icon-{id}` (same markup from `valueIconMarkup()` / `VALUE_ICON_DEFS.cls` in `app.js`)
- Docs: `BRANDING-LAYOUT.md` → **Value icon color map**

## Never

- Separate colors for filter vs `.toc-value` (no parallel hex lists)
- Filter-only overrides that force a shared purple / white stroke on `.value-icon-key .value-icon`
- Hardcoded badge colors in `app.js`, `projects-data.js`, or project markdown

## When changing a color

Edit the `--vi-*` token once; confirm filter tile badge and table badge both update. Chip backgrounds use `--vi-*-chip` only — they do not replace badge fills.
